---
import { csReview } from "../lib/pilot-topics";
import { readingParagraphs } from "../lib/reading-paragraphs";
---
<p>The trial ranked {csReview.ranking.ranked_topics} topics in {csReview.ranking.ranked_categories} categories. Grouping checks failed for {csReview.ranking.group_review_failures} candidates and {csReview.ranking.fallback_summaries} ranked summaries used fallback text. The examples below keep their original ranks and link every supporting paper.</p>
  <p>After the field criteria were revised, the classifier matched {csReview.classification_checks.final.fresh_matches} of {csReview.classification_checks.final.fresh} previously unseen cases. It placed a study of relationships among AI companies in information science. That paper contributed to none of the ranked topics.</p>
  <ol>{csReview.selected_topics.map(topic => <li value={topic.rank} tabindex="-1" id={`review-${csReview.edition}-${topic.rank}`}>
    <h3>{topic.headline}</h3>{readingParagraphs(topic.reviewed_summary).map(paragraph => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
    <details><summary aria-label={`Supporting papers (${topic.papers.length}) for rank ${topic.rank}`}>Supporting papers ({topic.papers.length})</summary>
      <ul>{topic.papers.map(paper => <li><a href={paper.url}>{paper.title}</a></li>)}</ul>
    </details>
  </li>)}</ol>
